    <string name="cable_hint">One phone may ask to allow Wamda to access the device; accept it. If nothing happens, flip the cable around.</string>
    <string name="cable_steps_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="cable_steps">A USB-C cable directly between the phones. One acts as USB host, the other as accessory; Wamda picks the roles. Speed depends on the port: about 30 MB/s on USB 2.0, far more on USB 3. With Wi-Fi connected at the same time, both paths are used together.</string>
